---
import Doc from '@/layouts/Doc.astro'
import Command from '@/components/Command.astro'
import CodeSwitcher from '@/components/CodeSwitcher.astro'
import PromptLabels from '@/components/PromptLabels.astro'
---

<Doc
  title="Prompts"
  description="Versioned prompts with labels such as production and staging, fetched and rendered by the SDKs, cached in the process, and linked to the steps that used them."
  lede="Change a prompt without a deploy, and see which version wrote each answer."
  og="docs"
>
  <h2>Versions and labels</h2>
  <p>
    A prompt is a name and a list of versions. A version is a text template or a
    list of chat messages, with <code>{'{{variable}}'}</code> placeholders and
    the model settings you want stored beside it. A version never changes once
    stored; a new body is a new version, numbered by the daemon. Posting a body
    identical to the latest version stores nothing, so a deploy that posts its
    prompts on every start is a no-op when nothing changed.
  </p>
  <p>
    A label points at one version. Your code fetches by label, usually
    <code>production</code>, so releasing a prompt is moving the label to the
    new version and rolling it back is moving it to the old one. Neither needs
    a deploy. <code>latest</code> is reserved and always means the newest
    version.
  </p>

  <PromptLabels class="not-prose my-8" />

  <Command
    class="not-prose my-6"
    title="store a version, then release it"
    command={`curl -X POST localhost:4317/v1/api/prompts \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"name": "support/reply", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Answer {{customer}} briefly."}]}'
curl -X PUT localhost:4317/v1/api/prompts/support%2Freply/labels/production \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"version": 1}'`}
  />

  <h2>Fetching and rendering</h2>
  <p>
    Each SDK fetches a prompt by name and label and renders it with your
    variables in the process; the daemon never renders one. With no label and
    no version the SDK asks for <code>production</code>, and falls back to the
    latest version when no version carries it. A variable the prompt names and
    you did not pass is an error naming it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Fetched prompts are cached for 60 seconds by default. After that the SDK
    fetches again, and if the daemon does not answer it keeps serving the copy
    it has, so an outage does not stop an agent that fetched once. Pass a
    fallback template for the first start, before anything was fetched.
  </p>

  <CodeSwitcher
    class="not-prose my-6"
    only={['typescript', 'python', 'rust', 'go', 'kotlin', 'elixir']}
    region="prompt"
    title="fetch, render, link"
  />

  <h2>Linking a step to its prompt</h2>
  <p>
    Link the model span to the prompt it ran and the span carries
    <code>mcpd.prompt.name</code> and <code>mcpd.prompt.version</code>.
    <code>GET /v1/api/spans?prompt=support/reply&amp;prompt_version=2</code>
    lists every step that ran version 2, which is how a regression after a
    release is traced back to the change that caused it.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    The Prompts screen lists every prompt at its latest version. Open one to
    read each version, what changed from the one before, the labels on it and
    the steps that ran it, to move a label, and to store a new version.
  </p>

  <h2>Endpoints</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>GET /v1/api/prompts</code>: every prompt at its latest version.</li>
    <li><code>POST /v1/api/prompts</code>: store a version.</li>
    <li><code>GET /v1/api/prompts/{'{name}'}</code>: one version, by <code>label</code> or <code>version</code>.</li>
    <li><code>GET /v1/api/prompts/{'{name}'}/versions</code>: every version, newest first.</li>
    <li><code>PUT</code> and <code>DELETE /v1/api/prompts/{'{name}'}/labels/{'{label}'}</code>: move or remove a label.</li>
  </ul>
</Doc>
